{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a8402fc7cc240893","type":"text","text":"Since $R_2$ and $C_2$ are in series connection, just add them:\n$$ Z_2(s)= R_2 + \\frac{1}{C_2s} $$","x":-45,"y":-640,"width":320,"height":140,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"1b2a15730942c465","type":"text","text":"Substitute the values:\n$$\n\\boxed{Z_2(s) = 220k + \\frac{1}{0.1\\micro s}}\n$$","x":-55,"y":-380,"width":340,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b3207d58a2bc0ac8","type":"file","file":"Feedback/assets/Pasted image 20260910165414.png","x":-600,"y":-410,"width":446,"height":280},
		{"id":"7c5e08f6a544cebb","type":"text","text":"convert into impedance of components:\n\nFor resistors:\n$\\boxed{R = R}$\n\nFor capacitors:\n$C = {Cs}^{-1}$\n$\\boxed{C=\\frac{1}{Cs}}$","x":-497,"y":-900,"width":240,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"4b718ab3ad2d0835","type":"text","text":"Since $C_1$ and $R_1$ are parallel in  connection, add their reciprocals\n$$\nZ_1(s) = \\frac\n{1}\n{\n  \\frac{1}{1/C_1s}\n  + \\frac{1}{R_1}\n}\n$$","x":-1090,"y":-580,"width":260,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3d4599c9e0926171","type":"text","text":"substitute the impedance values:\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n Z_1(s) = \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{1/C_1s}+\\frac{1}{R_1}}\\\\\n Z_s(s) = \\frac{1}{C_1s+\\frac{1}{R_1}}\\\\\\\\\n Z_s(s) = \\frac{1}{5.6\\micro s +\\frac{1}{360k}}\\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n$$","x":-1110,"y":-320,"width":300,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b9c5857c59797636","type":"text","text":"Multiply both sides by 360k to remove the fraction inside the fraction","x":-1440,"y":5,"width":250,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"72af8bd781f3559e","type":"text","text":"Simplify the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left(\\frac{1}{5.6\\micro s +\\frac{1}{{\\color{yellow}360k}}}\\right)\n  \\left( {\\color{yellow}\\frac{360k}{360k}} \\right)\\\\\\\\\n\\frac{360k}{(5.6\\micro s)(360k) + \\frac{360k}{360k}}\\\\\\\\\n\\frac{360k}{(5.6\\micro s)(360k) + 1}\\\\\n\n\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\boxed{Z_1(s)=\\frac{360k}{(5.6\\micro s)(360k) + 1}}\\\\\n$$","x":-1140,"y":55,"width":360,"height":320,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"0b5f87bf49600783","type":"text","text":"To find the transfer function use the formula output over input:\n# $\\frac{V_{out}(s)}{V_{in}(s)}=-\\frac{Z_2(s)}{Z_1(s)}$","x":-5,"y":110,"width":240,"height":210,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ec5a0436f886cc82","type":"text","text":"$$\n-\\frac{220k+\\frac{1}{0.1\\micro s}}\n{\\frac{360k}{(5.6\\micro s)(360k)+1}}\n$$\nReplace units $k$ and $\\micro$ with the engineering notation:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{220\\times10^{3}+\\frac{1}{0.1s \\times10^{-6}}}\n{\\frac{360\\times10^{3}}{(5.6s\\times10^{-6})(360\\times10^3)+1}}\n$$\n\nSimplify some terms:\n$$\n-\\frac{220\\times10^{3}+\\frac{1}{0.1s \\times10^{-6}}}\n{\\frac{360\\times10^{3}}{{\\color{yellow}(5.6s\\times10^{-6})(360\\times10^3)}+1}}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n-\\frac{220\\times10^{3}+\\frac{1}{0.1s \\times10^{-6}}}\n{\\frac{360\\times10^{3}}{{\\color{yellow}2,016s\\times10^{-3}}+1}}\n$$\nEvaluate numerator by adding the fraction\n$$\n-\\frac{{\\color{yellow}220\\times10^{3}}+\\frac{1}{\\color{yellow}{0.1s \\times10^{-6}}}}\n{\\frac{360\\times10^{3}}{2,016s\\times10^{-3}+1}}\n$$\n\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\frac{{\\color{yellow} 22s\\times10^{-3}}+1}{0.1s \\times10^{-6}}}\n{\\frac{360\\times10^{3}}{2,016s\\times10^{-3}+1}}\n$$\nSimplify the fraction, multiply mo yung nasa taas at baba, thn multiply yung palaman ng fraction\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\frac{{\\color{green}22s\\times10^{-3}+1}}{\\color{yellow}0.1s \\times10^{-6}}}\n{\\frac{\\color{yellow}360\\times10^{3}}{\\color{green}2,016s\\times10^{-3}+1}}\n$$\nSimplify the engineering notations\n$$\n-\\frac{\\color{green}(22s\\times 10^{-3}+1)(2,016s\\times10^{-3}+1)}\n{\\color{yellow}(0.1s\\times10^{-6})(360\\times10^3)}\n$$\nEvaluate, multiply and use foil method\n$$\n-\\frac{(0.022s+1)(2.016s+1)}\n{(0.1s\\times10^{-6})(360,000)}\n$$\ncombine similar terms\n$$\n-\\frac{0.044352s^2 + 0.022s + 2.016s + 1}\n{0.036s}\n$$\nremove the coefficient of denominator by multiplying it to $\\frac{1}{0.036}$:\n$$\n-\\frac{0.044352s^2 + 2.038s + 1}\n{\\color{yellow}0.036s}\n\\left( \\frac{\\frac{1}{\\color{yellow}0.036}}{\\frac{1}{\\color{yellow}0.036}} \\right)\n$$\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\frac{0.044352}{0.036}s^2 + \\frac{2.038}{0.036}s + \\frac{1}{0.036}}\n{\\frac{0.036}{0.036}s}\n$$\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1.232s^2 + 56.61s + 27.78}\n{s}\n$$\nFactor out the coefficient of $s^2$:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{\\color{yellow}1.232}(\\frac{1.232s^2}{\\color{yellow}1.232} + \\frac{45.95s}{\\color{yellow}1.232} + \\frac{22.55}{\\color{yellow}1.232})}\n{s}\n$$\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1.232(s^2 + 45.95s + 22.55)}\n{s}\n$$\n\nClean up the fraction:\n$$\n\\boxed{\\frac{V_{out}(s)}{V_{in}(s)}=-1.232\\frac{s^2 + 45.95s + 22.55}\n{s}}\n$$\n","x":480,"y":-1080,"width":440,"height":1520,"color":"6"}
	],
